{
  "id": "aperture_frame",
  "version": "1.0.0",
  "comment": "Emit seeds/aperture_frame.json -- APERTURE IS A FRAME: chosen, forced, or negotiated.\n\n`observer_aperture` made aperture graph data, but as a single authored list on the\nobserver -- an acuity it simply HAS. That is incomplete. An aperture is a FRAME\nyou are viewing in, and a frame has provenance: you can choose it, it can be\nforced on you, or you can negotiate it with someone else.\n\nThis is the reference-frame sense, not the Fillmore `Frame` (which is language\nsemantics and is left alone). And it is not a metaphor here: `CLAUDE.md`'s\nframe/continuum invariant puts every lossy or real-valued map in\n`Hom(frame, frame)` rather than inside a frame's coordinates, and the projection\n`observer_aperture` performs IS such a map -- world frame to observer frame, with\nthe collapse marker naming exactly what the map discards.\n\nTwo things follow, and the second is the whole point.\n\n**The effective aperture is a MEET.** Every frame in force narrows what you\nresolve, so `resolves` stops being authored and becomes derived: the fold of\n`Intersect` over your own maximum acuity and every frame currently on you. An\nobserver declares its PHYSIOLOGY (`ap_full`); the frames decide the rest.\n\n**The three modes decode identically and differ entirely in RECOURSE.** This is\nthe testable content -- same residual, three different things you may do about it:\n\n  * CHOSEN -- you narrowed your own attention, so you may widen it unilaterally.\n    An outstanding residual is a reason to look harder, and `ap_relax_chosen`\n    drops the frame and re-arms the decode. Attention, mechanically.\n  * FORCED -- someone or something else narrowed it, and you cannot lift it. An\n    outstanding residual here is a gap you can DETECT and cannot close alone, so\n    it opens a `SelfConcern` on the existing human-gated spine. This is the\n    knowing-THAT-without-knowing-WHAT case from `ONE_LOOP_MANY_GRAINS.md`, one\n    level up: not merely unresolved, but unresolvable BY YOU.\n  * NEGOTIATED -- it binds several parties, so no one may change it alone. A\n    proposal takes effect only when every bound party has accepted; a unilateral\n    accept does nothing at all.\n\nAn agent that can only be forced has no attention; one that can only choose has\nno social constraint; one that cannot negotiate cannot establish common ground.\n",
  "depends_on": [
    "observer_aperture"
  ],
