      "comment": "The effective aperture is the MEET of the observer's own maximum acuity and every frame in force on it, whatever the provenance. `resolves` is therefore DERIVED, not authored: an observer declares its physiology (`ap_full`) and the frames decide the rest. Re-arms on any change in how many frames are in force -- which is what makes dropping a chosen frame actually widen perception.",
